  "interpretation": [
    "The device-free EQ slice reproduces a substantial cost increase when gains change, with no relay or CC scaling intermediaries present.",
    "Fixed flat and non-flat audio averaged 52.377 us and 30.292 us of calling-thread CPU. Updating all gains directly averaged 3766.034 us, of which direct setters accounted for only 2.082 us.",
    "MIDI changes to all gains averaged 2224.671 us at frame zero and 2428.133 us with events spread across the block. Individual-band change scenarios averaged 1818.821-3104.545 us. Silence plus gain changes also incurred 2845.416 us on average.",
    "The fixed non-flat control sets all gains to Carla's calibrated value for MIDI 96. Its low steady cost distinguishes gain-change work from merely running the EQ with non-unity gains.",
    "CPU-time growth remains when MIDI mapping is bypassed and occurs mainly during the subsequent audio block. This narrows the investigation to the hosted EQ parameter-refresh/processing path; it does not establish a specific LSP or Carla defect.",
    "All scenarios stayed below the nominal 21.33 ms block duration in this local run. There is no audio server or realtime deadline here, so this is not proof that Airstar's live graph is stable.",
    "CPU frequency, load, and scenario order are not controlled. Do not rank faders or infer a precise direct-versus-MIDI speed ratio from this run.",
    "Carla emitted one known Filter select bounds warning and hidden-UI parameter notifications. No plugin UI was opened. Direct-setter timing includes synchronous notification work; any asynchronous work remains outside the calling-thread measurement."
  ],
